// declarations: the front end rather than the VM. clock() is process CPU time
// since start, so reading it in the first statement of the file measures
// startup plus scanning and compiling everything below it -- 20000 function
// declarations, each with a body, a parameter list and its own constants.
//
// This is the one benchmark that cannot be repeated: compilation finished
// before the first statement ran, and nothing in the language can compile
// source again. Mean, min and max are one sample, and there is no n_runs to
// scale; to make it longer, generate more declarations.

var elapsed = clock();

